\section{4. Cleaning and Preprocessing}

We prepare the raw stream in four sequential stages:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Schema Normalization:} GBFS payloads occasionally duplicate keys across camelCase and snake\_case representations (e.g., \texttt{numDocksAvailable} vs. \texttt{num\_docks\_available}). We cast all attributes to standardized snake\_case and extract nested bike breakdown objects.
    \item \textbf{Operational Filtering:} We drop records where $\texttt{is\_installed} = 0$, or where both $\texttt{is\_renting} = 0$ and $\texttt{is\_returning} = 0$, ensuring technical outages are not misclassified as depleted or saturated stations.
    \item \textbf{Temporal Resampling and Weather Merging:} Station snapshots are rounded to uniform 15-minute intervals and enriched with corresponding hourly meteorological features.
    \item \textbf{Spatial Context Scoring:} Using station coordinates (\texttt{lat}, \texttt{lon}), we calculate geodesic proximity buffers to OpenStreetMap amenities, generating three contextual metrics: \texttt{university\_score}, \texttt{business\_score}, and \texttt{tourism\_score}.
\end{enumerate}

\section{5. Next Steps: Exploration and the Prediction Test}

Before modeling we will explore the data visually with an interactive Folium map of station capacities and activity zones, average availability curves for weekdays versus weekends, and heatmaps of saturation by neighborhood across the week.

We define a station as \textbf{critical} if it has at most one bike available or at most one free dock. We then compare two supervised classification models that predict criticality 15 minutes ahead. \textbf{Model A (baseline)} uses current bike and dock counts, first-order differences ($\Delta_{t-15}$), cyclic hour/day features, and weather variables. \textbf{Model B (context-aware)} augments Model A with the three spatial density scores. Evaluating precision, recall, and AUROC across both models will determine whether surrounding urban geography provides distinct predictive signal beyond short-term station momentum.

